# args: --eval=nope
# A name nothing bound is a deferred global at the prompt, so this compiles and
# then fails where it runs: stdout stays empty and the traceback is the one the
# prompt prints. The status is 1, which is the status `printf 'nope\n' |
# jaithon repl` ends with: --eval shares the REPL's evaluator, so it has to
# share the REPL's verdict on what it evaluated.
print("stdin was read")
